src/oracles/Curve2TokenOracle.sol:_lpTokenValue:75|C23|Medium|The hardcoded coin-index set {0,1} (coins(0)/coins(1) in the constructor, balances(0)/balances(1) and fixed length-2 arrays in _lpTokenValue) is never validated against the pool's N_COINS, so an oracle constructed over a 3-coin Curve stableswap-NG/factory pool — which exposes the identical coins(uint256)/balances(uint256)/get_dy(int128,int128,uint256) ABI and is its own LP token, so construction and every read succeed silently — divides only coins 0+1 by the full pool totalSupply, permanently under-pricing the LP by ~1/N with no revert and no downstream backstop, letting any unprivileged liquidator seize healthy vault positions at a fabricated ~33% discount.|src/oracles/Curve2TokenOracle.sol
